 "id": "2026-11-03-us-floods-florida-southwest",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Florida got a so-called thousand-year rain. The Southwest is flooding too. Why?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "In Melbourne, Florida, more than eleven inches fell in one day, a record, the National Weather Service says. Parts of southern Brevard County saw over twenty inches, forecasters reported. Officials counted more than two hundred high-water rescues, and Florida declared a state of emergency."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Out west, a storm dropped months of rain in days. Evacuations reached at least a dozen counties in Arizona, Colorado, Utah and New Mexico, the Associated Press reports. Arizona's governor declared a statewide emergency. One person died, and a man is missing in Flagstaff."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "So why now? Climate scientist Daniel Swain says back-to-back events in a strong El Niño are no coincidence. A NOAA meteorologist says it can't yet be tied to El Niño."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will more of the U.S. flood this month? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
